From 05d22edb8cba4242f923fd1ac2a04891e88d070d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 78andyp <drandypowell@live.co.uk>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 17:05:22 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [video] Stop choosing art when the art type list isn't
 confirmed

Exiting Kodi while the list of art types was open hung the GUI thread.
Once the application stops, a modal dialog returns without being closed,
and the list still reports the type it pre-selected. Choose art took
that as a choice, opened the image browser, which also returned at once,
and showed the list again, forever. Exiting from the image browser hung
the same way.

The list is now only acted on when an art type was confirmed or "Add art
type" was pressed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 xbmc/video/dialogs/GUIDialogVideoInfo.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/xbmc/video/dialogs/GUIDialogVideoInfo.cpp b/xbmc/video/dialogs/GUIDialogVideoInfo.cpp
index 8577dc4..f89adb4 100644
--- a/xbmc/video/dialogs/GUIDialogVideoInfo.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/video/dialogs/GUIDialogVideoInfo.cpp
@@ -947,6 +947,8 @@ bool CArtTypeChooser::ChooseArtType()
   dialog->SetItems(m_items);
   dialog->SetSelected(m_selectedItem);
   dialog->Open();
+  if (!dialog->IsConfirmed() && !dialog->IsButtonPressed())
+    return false;
   m_selectedItem = dialog->GetSelectedItem();
 
   if (dialog->IsButtonPressed())
-- 
